  "id": "USN-8979-2",
  "summary": "deluge vulnerabilities",
  "details": "USN-8979-1 fixed vulnerabilities in Deluge. Due to a packaging error, the\nfixes were not applied in the update for Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. This update\nfixes the problem.\n\nOriginal advisory details:\n\n It was discovered that the web UI in Deluge did not protect against\n cross-site request forgery. A remote attacker could possibly use this\n issue to trick a user into installing a malicious plugin, resulting in the\n execution of arbitrary code. (CVE-2017-7178)\n\n It was discovered that the web UI in Deluge incorrectly handled certain\n requests. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\n arbitrary files. (CVE-2017-9031)",
